  "narrative": "No discovery assessments are due, no validation response deadline is present, and the voluntary validation budget is exhausted. For these new discovery claims, acceptance will therefore require a signed 95% Welch lower bound above the outcome-specific threshold of 0.15 composite dependency-score units in the registered direction; lower bounds below threshold should not be interpreted as threshold-relevant even if the point estimate is large. For direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the raw feature_037 exposure-minus-comparator contrast is negative, i.e. feature_037=1 is associated with lower outcome_001 and stronger composite dependency in this supplied dataset.\n\nI registered six direct conditional stability tests for the dominant predictors. The first three test feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 within the strong feature_063-context region feature_038>=0 together with feature_018<=0. This joint context is scientifically central because feature_063 is already well supported as reverse-associated with outcome_001 under exactly this context (H197/R158 and related accepted claims). The hypothesis is that the dominant associations remain threshold-relevant and approximately additive in this context: feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 should remain associated with higher outcome_001, while feature_037=1 should remain associated with lower outcome_001. Plausible alternatives are context-specific attenuation or saturation, especially if the joint feature_038/feature_018 context selects a region where outcome_001 is already strongly shifted by feature_063-related structure; in that case the point estimate could fall below 0.15 or the interval could fail to support acceptance.\n\nThe next three proposals test the same dominant predictors within feature_060=1. This is a newly supported feature_063 context (H287/R247), though with a small feature_063-exposed cell. Direct dominant-predictor tests in feature_060=1 ask whether feature_060=1 is merely a context for feature_063 modification or whether it also changes the main dominant-predictor structure. The expected result is persistence of the large feature_010, feature_002, and feature_037 effects. A failure to reach threshold, or reversal toward null, would support broader context dependence and would justify deferring any simple additive model for the supplied dataset.\n\nTo keep the analysis queue focused, I deferred six already active but lower-priority rare binary main-effect screens (H52, H53, H54, H55, H56, H100) rather than closing them. They remain unresolved and can be reactivated later if the current broad screens and dominant-context stability tests complete. I retained the more prevalent and context-relevant binary screens (H45 feature_060, H46 feature_035, H48 feature_033, H49 feature_016, H50 feature_013, and H51 feature_064) in the active set. All conclusions remain dataset-specific observational associations, not causal, mechanistic, biological, or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 22 explore. Validation requests exhausted; any accepted future claims must be supported by discovery evidence alone and judged against signed lower bounds >0.15 in registered direction.\n\nCurrent robust dataset-specific structure: feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 are strongly associated with higher outcome_001; feature_037=1 is strongly associated with lower outcome_001 (stronger composite dependency). Dominant interactions are mostly near zero or rejected, supporting approximate additivity. Research markers feature_007/058/015 are clean nulls. Feature_063 is context-dependent: global reverse association is unresolved (discovery/validation lower bounds just below 0.15), but accepted conditional reverse contexts include clean dominant-zero, feature_010=0, feature_037=0, feature_002=0, feature_038>=0, feature_018<=0, combined feature_038>=0 with feature_018<=0, feature_033=1, and feature_060=1 (latter narrow).\n\nAnalysis queue adjustment: deferred rare binary screens H52, H53, H54, H55, H56, H100; retained H45, H46, H48, H49, H50, H51. Added six direct stability tests: feature_010, feature_002, feature_037 within (feature_038>=0 AND feature_018<=0), and within feature_060=1. These test whether dominant effects remain threshold-relevant in important accepted feature_063 contexts. If accepted, they strengthen additive dominant structure. If attenuated/null, treat feature_038/018/060 as broader context modifiers.\n\nRemaining uncertainty: global feature_063 reverse association, feature_003 context, feature_004/026 weak signals, continuous signature dose-response, and many untested/rare binary predictors. Future tests should avoid very small feature_063 cells unless necessary, and all claims remain non-causal and non-generalizable."
